BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/the-art-of-wellbeing-therapeutic-art-making-in-the-museum/2026-09-19/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T113000
DTSTAMP:20260914T145714Z
CREATED:20260609T163004Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260914T145714Z
UID:10006913-1789812000-1789817400@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:The Art of Wellbeing: Therapeutic Art Making in the Museum
DESCRIPTION:Art has the power to heal\, restore\, and reconnect us to what matters most. Join us at the Asheville Art Museum for a guided art-making session led by a registered art therapist\, designed to explore how art can be a tool to nurture your mental and emotional wellbeing. Whether you’re a seasoned artist or have never picked up a paintbrush\, come as you are and leave feeling refreshed. Join Alexis for sessions on August 15\, September 19\, and December 19. \nDr. C. Alexis Decosimo is a licensed mental health clinician\, registered art therapist\, and Doctor of Public Health. She specializes in helping children\, families\, and individuals access healing through blending therapeutic artmaking and evidence-based approaches including EMDR\, cognitive behavioral therapy\, and person-centered approaches.\nShe believes in meeting clients where they are\, drawing on creative modalities to open pathways to healing that talk therapy alone may not reach. Her clinical work is deeply informed by over a decade of international experience building mental health programs in some of the world’s most under-resourced settings\, giving her a grounded\, adaptive\, and culturally sensitive approach to care.\nIn her Asheville practice\, she brings that same commitment to accessible\, ethical\, and community-rooted mental health support to help clients process trauma\, build resilience\, and find their footing through the power of expressive therapy.   For more information follow: Ashevillearttherapy.com \nPurchase Tickets \nPlease enter through the Staff Entrance to the left of the building.
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/the-art-of-wellbeing-therapeutic-art-making-in-the-museum/2026-09-19/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Wellness
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/AF2024-Insta-Drafts-Presentation-e1732724872483.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Livemusicasheville": "https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/heritage-weekend-2/2026-09-19/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:livemusicasheville
X-SOURCE:LiveMusicAsheville.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T160000
DTSTAMP:20260914T170243Z
CREATED:20260914T170052Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260914T170243Z
UID:10021345-1789812000-1789833600@livemusicasheville.com
SUMMARY:The Southern Highland Craft Guild's 46th Annual Heritage Weekend
DESCRIPTION:You are invited to our 46th. annual Heritage Weekend on September 19 and 20 at the Folk Art Center on the Blue Ridge Parkway. \nMany of you have been to this fun event in the past and we will again host over 20 heritage artist\, musicians and dancers to honor and celebrate Mountain Heritage Crafts. \nOne of the highlights of the celebration is our Annual World Gee Haw Whimmy Diddle competition on Saturday afternoon. \nA Whimmy Diddle is an Appalachian mountain toy\, traditionally made from 2 sticks  of rhododendron. Notches are carved into the stick and a propeller is attached to the end. Rubbing the notches with the second stick makes the propeller spin! The trick is to make it spin gee (to the right) or haw (to the left). \nContestants are judged by their skills and interesting prizes will be awarded. \nThe music stage will provide entertainment with Blue Grass and Gospel music\, and cloggers will demonstrate the mountain dance tradition. \n\n\n\nFolk Art Center\, Blue Ridge Parkway\n\n\nCome for the craft\, stay for the music!\n\n\n\n\nEntertainment Schedule: \nLive Bluegrass and Mountain Music performances on an outdoor stage\n\nSaturday\, Sept. 19 \n10 a.m. – Ash Woody- Appalachian Jack Tales\n11 a.m. – Michael and Donna Fox \n12 p.m.- Blue-Eyed Girl\n1 p.m. – Split Rail\n2 p.m. – 46th Annual World Gee Haw Whimmy Diddle Competition\n3 p.m. – Carol Rifkin and Friends \nSunday\, Sept. 20\n11 a.m. – Davy Arch- Cherokee Stories\n12 p.m. – Nobody’s Darlin’ Stringband\n1 p.m. – Jonah Riddle and Carolina Express\n2 p.m. – Buncombe Turnpike\n3 p.m. – Janet Wiseman and Pearl Shirley – Mountain Music
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/heritage-weekend-2/2026-09-19/
LOCATION:Folk Art Center\, Blue Ridge Parkway
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/799773895_1079489951705543_5534703578023715376_n-e1789405354556.jpg
END:VEVENT
