X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Haywood County Walking Meetup Group": "https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/events/316043156/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_haywood_county_walking_meetup_group
X-SOURCE:Haywood County Walking Group
UID:event_316043156@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260919T042008Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T120000
SUMMARY:Biltmore Estate: Walk the Westover Black Trails
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nLocated at The Inn on Bil
 tmore Estate\, the Westover Black Trails provide access to some of Biltmor
 e's beautiful woodlands. We will loop the Black Trail in a counterclockwis
 e direction.\n\nBiltmore says it is 3.5 miles. The Black Trail is narrow. 
 It is a moderately difficult trail. There is elevation change\, but just a
  bit strenuous. (For those who have walked the Green and Blue Trails\, the
 re is less chance for confusion.)\n\nWhen you drive to the Inn\, you will 
 turn onto its access road. Near the entrance to the Inn is the entrance to
  the parking area. There are two rows of parking\, an upper row closer to 
 the Inn\, and a lower row a little further from the Inn. We will gather on
  the lower row at the far end (away from the Inn).\n\nIf you need a restro
 om prior to the walk\, Antler Hill is very close and there are public rest
 rooms there. No restroom facilities are available during the walk.\n\nDres
 s appropriately for the weather. Tennis shoes are fine\, unless it has rai
 ned a lot recently\, in which case you will want light hiking boots. Walki
 ng sticks are desirable\; I plan to use two. As always\, bring plenty of w
 ater and a protein snack. Dogs on leash are welcome if they are accustomed
  to trail walking. Trail strollers would find this a bit difficult.\n\nThe
 re is a grounds admission fee. We walk at Biltmore several times each year
 \, so an annual grounds pass is highly recommended.\n\nMany regular Biltmo
 re guests have never walked the Westover Trails. I think you will enjoy th
 ese.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/316043156/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260809T121739Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T121739Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/guided-trail-walk-3/2026-09-19/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T120000
DTSTAMP:20260710T074430Z
CREATED:20260710T074430Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260710T074430Z
UID:1778780019627-1789812000-1789819200@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Guided Trail Walk
DESCRIPTION:Hit the trails and learn more about The North Carolina Arboretum’s botanically diverse forest with a guided trail walk! April through October\, this free hiking program is led by trained volunteer guides who take small groups of participants along woodland trails and through a variety of forest types. Depending on the season and each guide’s area of expertise\, topics of discussion may include wildflowers\, plant and tree identification\, natural history and more. \nGuided trail walks are limited to 15 people\, including the guide\, and are not recommended for guests under 16 years of age. Groups depart from the Baker Visitor Center Lobby on Tuesdays at 1 p.m. and Saturdays at 10 a.m. and 1 p.m.. \nWalks last 1.5 – 2.5 hours\, are approximately one to two miles in length. As this program is held rain or shine\, all participants should dress appropriately for the weather. \nThere is no pre-registration; walks are first-come first served and sign up sheets are located in the Baker Visitors Center. \nWalks are FREE; however\, donations to The North Carolina Arboretum Society are appreciated. Regular parking fees apply. Arboretum Society Members always park free. \nKnow Before You Go\n\nGuided Trail Walks are not recommended for guests under 16 years of age.\nGuided Trail Walks are rain or shine and all participants should be dressed comfortably and for the weather.\nHikes cover 1-2 miles and last 1.5-2 hours.\nWell-behaved leashed pets are welcome to accompany their owners. In the rare case that a pet is disruptive or negatively impacts the experience\, the pet and its owner may be asked to excuse themselves from the guided walk.
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/guided-trail-walk-3/2026-09-19/
CATEGORIES:Guided Trail Walk
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Birders-on-Cove-Hardwood-Trail-GSMNP-TN-Apr-16-1-1-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/monarch-butterfly-day-4/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T150000
DTSTAMP:20260916T163615Z
CREATED:20260805T162709Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260916T163615Z
UID:1778780019717-1789812000-1789830000@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Monarch Butterfly Day
DESCRIPTION:Monarch Butterfly Day\nSeptember 19\, 2026\n10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m.\nJoin us at The North Carolina Arboretum on Sept 19th for a day dedicated to the Monarch Butterfly!\nEach fall\, the last monarch butterflies of the year pass through Western North Carolina on their incredible migration to Mexico. Join us on Saturday\, September 19\, for a day dedicated to celebrating monarchs\, pollinators\, and the communities that connect us to the outdoors. \nFrom 10:00 a.m.–3:00 p.m.\, enjoy hands-on activities with community partners and vendors\, crafts and activities in the Playing Woods\, a StoryWalk\, guided pollinator walks\, Lotería\, dance performances\, and more. \nThis year’s Monarch Day is extra special as Latinos Aventureros joins us to celebrate not only the monarchs\, but also their 5th year of connecting communities across North Carolina to the outdoors through bilingual adventures\, health and wellness\, environmental conservation\, and youth programs. \nMonarch Day activities are free to attend.\nThe Arboretum’s standard parking fee applies to nonmembers. North Carolina Arboretum members park free as usual. \nSchedule\n10:00 a.m.–3:00 p.m: Community vendors\, activities & crafts\n10:30 am: Guided Pollinator Walk\n11:30 am: Dance Performance: Raíces\n12:30 pm: Lotería Salud y Aventura at the Education Center Veranda Lawn\n1:30 pm: Dance Performance: Mä Hñäkihu\n2:15 pm: Guided Pollinator Walk \nCome celebrate the remarkable journey of the monarch and a shared love of nature\, community\, and belonging! \nSponsored by: 
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/monarch-butterfly-day-4/
CATEGORIES:Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Stock-Monarch-Child-scaled-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
