X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_hendo_fun_friends
X-SOURCE:Hendo Fun Friends
UID:event_316555966@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260919T042009Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260924T091500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260924T150000
SUMMARY:Sam Knob\; a Saunter 
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nDarlene will lead to Sam Knob in the Black 
 Balsam area of the BRPwy\; Up to 12 of you are welcome.\nAfter a ½ mile w
 alk through the meadow. the climb is just shy of 400 ft. in ½ mile via se
 veral switchbacks on the trail. We pass a lush\, young forest of mostly no
 rthern hardwood trees. There are many roots and rocky areas along the trai
 l.\nLush vegetation grows near rock outcrops beside the trail\, including 
 blueberries\, strawberries\, sedges and grass\, mountain laurel\, Carolina
  rhododendron\, and countless wildflowers including bluets. The trail will
  pass beneath some large rock outcrops\, which lie just below the summit. 
 We’ll reach a grassy\, shrubby saddle between the two high knobs\, and a
  large outcropping of snow white quartz rocks from a grassy meadow.\nDiffi
 culty: Trail Tread Condition: Moderately Rough\; Constant moderate climb. 
 Rocky.\nWE WILL SPEND TIME FOR LUNCH AT THE TOP.\n**We are the Sloth Hike 
 Team of WNC: “We will get there when we get there.”**\n**https://www.y
 outube.com/watch?v=TQ8H4EK2vt4**\n**Social ‘hour’ at 9:15 AM. tires ro
 ll at 9:30AM**\nDistance: 3 mi RT\; Accum Ascent: 570 ft\; Pace: **1.25mph
 **\nDrive time: 45min/ 23 mi 1-way\nApprx return time: 3 PM\nCarpool contr
 ibutions appreciated. $3.00 suggested\n**THIS IS A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE.**
  This event is ***NOT*** for those who are uncomfortable with the antics o
 f fun-loving dogs. Well trained dogs **(you don’t have to yell)** can be
  'off-leash'. 'On leash' during the lunch stop. 'On leash' in vicinity of 
 other hike groups. Small (lap)dogs may carpool. Large dogs will drive them
 selves.\nWeather Check:\nhttps://www.mountain-forecast.com/peaks/Black-Bal
 sam-Knob/forecasts/1894\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN O
 N.\nI currently have 2 driver(s) (=8ppl)\nWe suggest slightly open windows
  while carpooling. Only you know your own health status so judge according
 ly if an event may endanger your health or the health of others.\nPlease b
 ring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy shoes into the dr
 iver's car at the end of the hike.\nAll hikes are at your own risk. You ar
 e responsible for your OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: The org
 anizer of this event is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The func
 tion of the organizer is only to organize this event. There are certain ri
 sks inherent in any outdoor activity. Each participant\, by signing up to 
 attend this event\, agrees to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo
  Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, 
 injury\, illness\, or personal loss which might occur while participating 
 in this activity or while traveling in any vehicle during this trip. **Eac
 h participant further agrees to abide by the rules and regulations concern
 ing safety\, to follow instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become i
 ntentionally separated from the group.** The leader(s) also has the right 
 to use any images collected on this trip for recording on website photo co
 llections.\ngordie's contact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(**BEFORE** day o
 f hike): 828.393.0297 (talk & text)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos
 /146993931@N05/albums**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/https-www-meetup-com-hendo-fun-friend
 s/events/316555966/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260914T170141Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260914T170141Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
