X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Warren Wilson College": "https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/sister-sadie-the-kittredge-arts-center-grand-reopening", "Asheville.com": "https://www.asheville.com/event/sister-sadie-the-kittredge-arts-center-grand-reopening", "Hendersonville.com": "https://www.hendersonville.com/event/sister-sadie-the-kittredge-arts-center-grand-reopening"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Calendar Ics": "https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/sister-sadie-the-kittredge-arts-center-grand-reopening"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_calendar_ics
X-SOURCE:Warren Wilson College, Asheville.com, Hendersonville.com
DTSTAMP:20260919T042029Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53886473896943
DTSTART:20261002T230000Z
DTEND:20261003T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:On Friday October 2nd at 7 PM\, Warren Wilson College celebrate
 s the grand reopening of Kittredge Arts Center\, with renowned Bluegrass a
 ct Sister Sadie headlining!  The Kittredge Arts Center grand reopening is 
 part of the Warren Wilson College's 2026 Homecoming\, and is also a homeco
 ming for Sister Sadie's mandolinist\, WWC alum' Rainy Miatke (Music Major\
 , Class of 2025). \n\n \n\nDoors open at 6:15 PM with light refreshments\,
  and concert starts at 7 PM.  \n\n \n\n \n\nTickets can be purchased here:
   https://wwc-ventures.ticketspice.com/sister-sadie-and-the-kittredge-arts
 -center-grand-reopening \n\n \n\nFor more information abuot the event\, pl
 ease contact Dr. Jason DeCristofaro at jdecristofaro@warren-wilson.edu or 
 (828)545-3916.  \n\n \n\n \n\nSister Sadie Bio:\n\nWhat started as an acci
 dental band became a force. GRAMMY-nominated. IBMA-decorated. Opry-validat
 ed. But for all the\naccolades\, they were often reduced to one line: an a
 ll-female bluegrass band. True—but never the point. Sister Sadie has alw
 ays\nbeen about the music. The fire. The truth.\n\n\nTheir new album\, All
  Will Be Well\, is that truth—loud\, fearless\, and free. You’ll hear 
 echoes of bluegrass\, but what rises is\nsomething bigger: country with cl
 aws\, Americana with muscle\, gospel grit and raw storytelling.\n\n\nFrom 
 the haunting “Prodigal Daughter” to the swagger of “Do What You Want
 ” and the aching beauty of “If I Don’t Have You\,”\nthese six wome
 n are not performing roles—they’re telling you who they are.\n\n\nThis
  is Sister Sadie\, evolved: bold\, bonded\, and braver than ever. They're 
 not asking for space. They're taking it.\n\n\nAnd they’re just getting s
 tarted.\n\n \n\nAbout Kittredge Arts Center:\n\nNestled within the beautif
 ul\, historic Warren Wilson College campus\, the Kittredge Arts Center pro
 vides a centralized location for the arts at WWC and WNC. The Center featu
 res the 321-seat Kittredge Theater and 80-seat Williams Recital Hall\, whe
 re music and performance events are featured throughout the year. Kittredg
 e Arts Center is also available as a rental space to organizations looking
  for an affordable option in a beautiful location for conferences\, busine
 ss retreats\, and other events. \n\n \n\nFor more information\, please con
 tact Dr. Jason DeCristofaro (Assistant Professor of Music\, Music Departme
 nt Chair\, and Director of Kittredge Arts Center) at 828-545-3916 or jdecr
 istofaro@warren-wilson.edu
GEO:35.613818;-82.438862
LOCATION:Kittredge Arts Center\, Kittredge Theater
SUMMARY:Sister Sadie & the Kittredge Arts Center Grand Reopening
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/sister-sadie-the-kittr
 edge-arts-center-grand-reopening
CATEGORIES:Performance
END:VEVENT
