UID:event_316598416@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260919T041953Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T141500
SUMMARY:Scenic AVL - Hendersonville - with WNC American Pilgrims on the Ca
 mino
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Overview:** This hike is offered
  as a monthly training hike with the WNC Asheville Chapter of the associat
 ion of American Pilgrims on the Camino. The route has been announced on th
 e WNC Camino Group [Facebook Group Page](https://www.facebook.com/groups/A
 VLCamino/announcements).\nIf you are unfamiliar with the Camino\, here are
  a few links to learn more:\n\n*[American Pilgrims on the Camino](https://
 americanpilgrims.org/iwpmap_directory/western-north-carolina/)\n- [Stingy 
 Nomads Camino](https://stingynomads.com/camino-de-santiago-walking-guide/)
 \n*[Gronze Camino Planner](https://www.gronze.com/)\n\n**Distance:** 5\, 7
 \, or 11 miles\n**Pace: 3.2 mph**\n\n**Start Times**\n**9:00 am**- Meet at
  First Congregational Church\, 1735 5th Ave W\, Hendersonville\, NC\n**10:
 45 - 11:00 - Southern Streams coffee across from the FCC church.**\n\nFirs
 t Section: The first section is a five mile loop. The loop ends at Souther
 n Streams coffee house\, which is across from the church where we start. J
 oin us here for coffee\, even if you don't have time to walk.\n\nSecond Se
 ction: Starting at about 11:15 am from Southern Streams coffee\, continue 
 through lower Laurel Park. For those who want to exit\, you can return to 
 the church on the Ecusta Trail for a total of about 7 miles.\n\nLast Secti
 on: To downtown and St. James Church\, returning via Ecusta Trail. 10.5 mi
 les total distance.\n\n**Caution:** There are a few stretches on busy road
 s where we will need to walk single file.\n\nFull Route: [Laurel Park Loop
 ](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/map/laurel-park-loop-improved-3937230?
 u=i&sh=ifwm3x)\n\nParking: We are meeting at the First Congregational Chur
 ch. Please carpool if possible.\n\nDogs: On leash the entire time. The fir
 st section is shady\, but the pavement may be hot on the last section. Ple
 ase consider your pup's feet in the heat.\n\nScenic Asheville Series: This
  hike counts as a Wildcard substitute on my Scenic Asheville Series. There
  are 9 [hikes](https://docs.google.com/document/d/11ewlUM9OV8I4npc1cNNsSYO
 nXI0QPw2isAleXdFzEbI/edit?usp=drivesdk) in the series\; hike them all and 
 receive an [attractive badge](https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/1goXUXfzU
 BqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit) for your backpack. Check your st
 atus [HERE](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW
 37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?gid=0#gid=0).\n\n**Questions**\nIf you have que
 stions\, call the hike leader (Gracen) at 828-290-0886.\n\n**Guests:** For
  this hike\, there are no guest restrictions. Bring them with you.\n\n**Di
 sclaimer and Release of Liability:**\nThis activity involves hiking on cit
 y streets that may have traffic and/or hiking on natural surfaces. Partici
 pants are responsible for their safety on streets and trails. The organize
 r of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function o
 f the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or participa
 te in this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to 
 assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a
  result of\, and associated with this event. You are responsible for any g
 uests\, dogs or other companions you bring with you. In addition\, you ack
 nowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms
 ](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316598416
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260917T164606Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260917T164606Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/the-art-of-presence-meditation-and-reflection-in-the-museum/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T110000
DTSTAMP:20260914T153329Z
CREATED:20260604T193214Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260914T153329Z
UID:10006746-1791019800-1791025200@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:The Art of Presence: Meditation and Reflection in the Museum
DESCRIPTION:Step into the Museum’s galleries before the doors open for a quiet and contemplative morning of meditation\, mindful walking\, and reflection. This guided experience invites participants to slow down\, settle the nervous system\, and explore the Museum as a place of sanctuary\, spaciousness\, and renewal. \nThe session will begin with a brief seated meditation\, followed by a walking meditation through selected exhibits. Along the way\, participants will pause with gentle mindfulness prompts designed to support personal reflection\, embodied awareness\, and a deeper connection with the artwork. Rather than offering art historical interpretation\, the experience encourages each participant to notice what arises within them through presence\, stillness\, and mindful seeing. The group will honor noble silence throughout much of the session with occasional opportunities for brief reflection and sharing. No previous meditation experience is needed. \nJoin Joshua on August 22\, October 3\, November 7\, and December 5. \nJoshua Canter is a mindfulness meditation teacher and the founder of True Nature Travels and Education\, an Asheville-based organization that has offered transformative retreats and educational experiences around the world for more than 20 years. He holds a master’s degree in Contemplative Psychology and is passionate about making mindfulness accessible\, grounded\, and relevant to everyday life. \nPurchase Tickets \nPlease enter through the Staff Entrance to the left of the building.
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/the-art-of-presence-meditation-and-reflection-in-the-museum/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Wellness
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/Screenshot-2026-03-31-at-1.17.55-PM-scaled.png
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Asheville Art Museum 2 South Pack Square Asheville NC 28801 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2 South Pack Square:geo:-82.5512827,35.5946714
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/bonsai-in-a-day-learn-create-take-home-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T163000
DTSTAMP:20260817T184406Z
CREATED:20260817T184406Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260817T184406Z
UID:1778780019765-1791019800-1791045000@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Bonsai in a Day: Learn\, Create\, Take Home
DESCRIPTION:Bonsai in a Day: Learn\, Create\, Take Home\nwith Rebecca Ayres \nSaturday\, October 3  |  9:30 am – 4:30pm \nRegister Here!\n  \nAlthough it has its roots in ancient Asian traditions\, the living art of bonsai now enjoys enthusiasts throughout much of the world. This class will provide the basic concepts and skills for novices to begin growing and shaping their own miniature trees. The first half of the class will cover the fundamental horticultural and aesthetic principles of bonsai. It will include such topics as tree selection\, watering\, pest control\, pruning\, wiring\, and styling. In the second half of the class\, each participant will receive a pot\, scissors\, wire\, and planting medium. With guidance from the instructor\, the students will create their own bonsai to take home. Materials included in registration. \nRebecca Ayres is a ceramic artist and gardener. A longtime Arboretum volunteer\, she is the assistant to the bonsai curator and helps with overseeing the exhibition garden\, the collection and the Carolina Bonsai Expo. She is a member of the Blue Ridge Bonsai Society\, where she has taught workshops and classes\, and is a graduate of the Arboretum’s Blue Ridge Naturalist program. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/bonsai-in-a-day-learn-create-take-home-2/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Bonsai-1024x576-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
