SUMMARY:Adult Studio: Beginner Drop Spinning
DESCRIPTION:Your life is filled with textiles made from various spun threads and yarn.  Come deepen those connections with the fibers that are deeply woven into many aspects  of our lives by trying your hand at one of the earliest ways to handspin yarn using a drop spindle.  Join us for a fun\, educational and meditative day of  learning the top whirl dropspindle\, and maybe some other styles as welll.  We will prepare\, card and spin raw wool fleece to create yarn on a drop spindle. You may have time to try different types of fibers and even different types of spindles.  You will get to take home your first handspun yarn\, as well as a drop spindle  to continue exploring this new skill. \nJamie Sparks is a multidisciplinary artist and educator with over 30 years of experience teaching learners of all ages. She has spent more than two decades working with natural fibers\, specializing in spinning and felting\, and has taught throughout the southeastern U.S.\, including the John C. Campbell Folk School\, Tryon Arts and Crafts School\, assisting at Penland School of Crafts and numerous arts councils.  Her fiber arts instruction emphasizes the transformation of raw fleece into finished pieces\, combining traditional techniques with an accessible\, hands-on approach. Jamie holds an Associates in Metalsmithing from Haywood Community College\, where she developed her skills in metalwork and design. Prior to her work in the arts\, she focused life as a herbal educator and plant biologist with a focus on the relationship between humans and plants—a passion that continues to influence her creative practice. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/adult-studio-beginner-drop-spinning/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Adult Studio
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/Jamie-Sparks-square-biowithspindle-web-1-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/naturalist-walk-and-talk-spiders/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T150000
DTSTAMP:20260903T174758Z
CREATED:20260819T165234Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260903T174758Z
UID:1778780019772-1791032400-1791039600@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Naturalist Walk and Talk - Spiders
DESCRIPTION:Naturalist Walk and Talk – Spiders\nwith Shane Myers \nSaturday\, October 3  |  1 – 3pm \nBRN – Elective \nRegister Here!\n  \nWalk around the Arboretum with our staff naturalists and talk about what we see around us. We might see plants and animals\, and evidence of them going about their lives in our backyard. Topics will be based on what we see and experience and whatever questions that come up\, so every class has the potential to be quite different. \nThis month we will focus on the Spiders of the Arboretum. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nShane Myers’ interest in nature began as a child with a love of dinosaurs. This quickly grew to include fossils\, insects\, and reptiles\, and learning from the notes his grandparents kept of the birds that came to their feeders in Toledo\, Ohio.  He has a Bachelors of Science in Wildlife Biology and did most of his undergraduate work on dragonflies and damselflies. He’s assisted in outreach and education for plant conservation groups\, Odonata Groups\, and various bird groups. Shane currently works for the Adult Education department at the NC Arboretum. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! \n●  Join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/naturalist-walk-and-talk-spiders/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education,BRN
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Adult-Ed-Course-Jpgs-51.png
END:VEVENT
