X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Haywood County Walking Meetup Group": "https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/events/315761287/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_haywood_county_walking_meetup_group
X-SOURCE:Haywood County Walking Group
UID:event_315761287@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260919T042008Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T153000
SUMMARY:Millpond Connector at Haywood Community College on National Taco D
 ay
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nAs we enter Leaf Season\,
  the temperature may indeed be cooler. Let's celebrate by going out for ta
 cos after the walk.\n\nTo get to the Millpond Connector from our start poi
 nt\, we will go clockwise on the Bobcat Trail and then take the Kingfisher
  Trail to the Copperhead Trail. When we intersect with the Millpond Connec
 tor\, we will turn left\, finishing the campus loop on the Bobcat Trail. A
 ltogether\, it isn't over 2 miles. Part of the walk is on pavement\, part 
 on well-groomed trail\, and part on not-as-well groomed trail. There is so
 me small elevation change.\n\nAs you enter the campus from Jones Cove Road
 \, go to the first parking lot on the left. We will gather there and then 
 head out.\n\nBe sure to dress for the weather. I'm going to wear tennis sh
 oes\, unless it has rained a lot recently (in which case\, I will wear lig
 ht hiking boots). I plan to bring one walking stick\, just in case. As alw
 ays\, you are urged to bring **plenty of water** and a protein snack. Dogs
  are welcome. Trail strollers should not have any problem. There are no ba
 throoms available on a Sunday afternoon\, so take care of such needs befor
 e you arrive.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/315761287/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260720T145351Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260720T145351Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Unca": "https://www.unca.edu/event/choosing-peace-after-loss-israel-palestine-civil-discourse-and-the-courage-to-listen/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:unca
X-SOURCE:UNC Asheville
DTSTART;TZID=America/Halifax:20261004T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Halifax:20261004T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T201120Z
CREATED:20260826T185419Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260902T201120Z
UID:10000128-1791122400-1791129600@www.unca.edu
SUMMARY:Choosing Peace After Loss: Israel/Palestine\, Civil Discourse\, and the Courage to Listen
DESCRIPTION:The UNC Asheville Center for Jewish Studies presents Aziz Abu Sarah\, co-author of “The Future Is Peace: A Shared Journey Across the Holy Land.” Drawing from his experiences and work in peacebuilding\, Abu Sarah will explore nonviolence\, dialogue\, shared humanity\, and the possibility of choosing peace after profound loss. \nThe presentation will be followed by a book signing. This event is free and open to the public and will take place in the Blue Ridge Room of Highsmith Student Union. \nClick here to register for this event. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Accessibility\nUNC Asheville is committed to providing universal access to all of our events. If you have any questions about access or would like to request reasonable accommodations that will facilitate your full participation in the film screenings\, please contact Stephanie Bullick\, Director of Accessibility\, at accessibility@unca.edu.
URL:https://www.unca.edu/event/choosing-peace-after-loss-israel-palestine-civil-discourse-and-the-courage-to-listen/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.unca.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Event-Calendar-TEMPLATE-11.png
END:VEVENT
