BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Unca": "https://www.unca.edu/event/birding-english-a-history-of-the-english-language-through-birds/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:unca
X-SOURCE:UNC Asheville
DTSTART;TZID=America/Halifax:20261015T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Halifax:20261015T191500
DTSTAMP:20260831T194737Z
CREATED:20260831T194736Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260831T194737Z
UID:10000129-1792087200-1792091700@www.unca.edu
SUMMARY:Birding English: A History of the English Language Through Birds
DESCRIPTION:Join Jeremy Withers\, Ph.D.\, of Iowa State University in the Laurel Forum (KAR 139) for a discussion of his new book\, “Birding English”\, which explains key moments in the history of the English language through birds. This event is ideal for word nerds and bird nerds alike! \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \nAccessibility\nUNC Asheville is committed to providing universal access to all of our events. If you have any questions about access or would like to request reasonable accommodations that will facilitate your full participation in the film screenings\, please contact Stephanie Bullick\, Director of Accessibility\, at accessibility@unca.edu.
URL:https://www.unca.edu/event/birding-english-a-history-of-the-english-language-through-birds/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.unca.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Event-Calendar-Graphic.png
END:VEVENT
