X-SOURCE:Books That Age Like Wine
UID:event_316083237@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260919T041959Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261208T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261208T203000
SUMMARY:The Leopard by Giuseppe Tomasi di Lampedusa
DESCRIPTION:Books That Age Like Wine\n**in 1860s Sicily\, Don Fabrizio Cor
 bera\, Prince of Salina\, remains skeptical and stoic as he faces civil wa
 r and his family's loss of wealth and status. The prince's favorite nephew
 \, Tancredi\, who opportunistically supports the unification efforts\, mar
 ries Angelica\, a beautiful woman from a lower social class\, to secure hi
 s future. This marriage symbolizes the shifting social order and the decli
 ne of the aristocracy. As Don Fabrizio struggles to adapt\, he retreats in
 to his love of astronomy\, finding solace in the unchanging stars while hi
 s world crumbles around him. Ultimately\, he must decide to resist the for
 ces of change or come to terms with them.**\n\n**Giuseppe Tomasi di Lamped
 usa\, the last in a line of Sicilian princes\, drew inspiration from his o
 wn family's decline to write this novel in the 1950s. The dramatic sweep a
 nd richness of Lampedusa’s observation\, his seamless intertwining of pu
 blic and private worlds\, and his sure grasp of human frailty imbue The Le
 opard with beauty and power.**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-classic-books-meetup-group/
 events/316083237/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260812T103331Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260812T103331Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
